UnitVotingRewardsManager::EarnedIncentives
├── given the program has not started
│   └── it should return zero
├── given the veNFT never voted
│   └── it should return zero
├── given another veNFT created global checkpoints
│   └── it should return zero for a veNFT with no checkpoint
├── given the checkpoint limit is zero
│   └── it should return zero
├── given only closed intervals exist
│   └── it should return the closed interval rewards
├── given the open interval is not yet closed
│   └── it should include the estimated open interval
├── given an open interval before the program starts
│   └── it should return zero
├── given the program starts inside the open interval
│   └── it should estimate only after the program starts
├── given the program ended before the latest global checkpoint
│   └── it should return only the program rewards
├── given the open interval crosses a week boundary
│   └── it should estimate the full unsettled interval
├── given the open interval exceeds the checkpoint iteration limit
│   └── it should return the full pending estimate
├── given the latest global checkpoint is mid week
│   └── it should match a later claim across the next week boundary
├── given a decaying open interval starts from a mid week global checkpoint
│   ├── it should estimate rewards using the weight share at the end of the interval
│   └── it should be lower than a claim at the same timestamp
├── given a bounded read over multiple user checkpoints
│   └── it should return only the bounded user checkpoints
├── given a bounded read stops before the latest user checkpoint
│   └── it should exclude the open interval
├── given a bounded read reaches the latest user checkpoint
│   └── it should include the estimated open interval
├── given the program ends inside the open interval
│   └── it should estimate only through the program end
├── given a non permanent decaying lock
│   └── it should return the decayed voting power share of closed intervals
├── given a decaying lock alongside a permanent lock
│   └── it should earn less than the permanent lock as its voting power decays
├── given a decaying lock alongside a permanent lock in the open interval
│   ├── it should estimate the decaying share
│   └── it should match a later claim approximately
├── given a decaying lock expires inside the open interval
│   ├── it should return only closed rewards
│   └── it should be lower than a claim at the same timestamp
├── given another decaying lock expires inside the open interval
│   ├── it should estimate rewards using the weight share at the end of the interval
│   └── it should be higher than a claim at the same timestamp
├── given a decaying lock expired before the open interval
│   └── it should ignore the open interval after expiry
├── given the latest user checkpoint is reset
│   └── it should ignore the open interval
├── given rewards were already partially claimed
│   └── it should return only the remaining closed rewards
└── given rewards were already partially claimed with a stale open interval
    └── it should return remaining rewards including the open interval
